※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4628 LANG_HANDED_OUT_GIVEN_BACK

※ An arena handed out with the answer is the caller's from the moment the function returns, so the
※ body may not give it back -- straight away or with `defer`: the caller would receive an answer
※ made in nothing.

fn named(n: u64) → str in pool:
    let pool: mut arena = ⎕arena
    defer ⎕empty(pool)
    "a" ⧺ "b" in pool

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let s: str in k = named(1u64)
    defer ⎕empty(k)
    if s = "ab": 0u6 else: 1u6
